hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1409","Abu Talib narrated to us Zayd bin Akhzam Al-Tai and Ibrahim bin Marzuq, they said: Wahb bin Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to me, he said: I heard Al-Numan. He is Ibn Rashid, narrating, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out One day he greeted us for rain and led us in prayer with two rak’ahs and aloud, without the call to prayer or iqamah.”"
